      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pelvicachromis-roloffi-2/",
      "html": "<p>P. roloffi is perhaps the rarest of all dwarf cichlids of the genus Pelvicachromis. It shows a clearly visible horizontal band in almost all moods. Males hardly grow larger than 8.5 cm; females always stay smaller.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pelvicachromis-roloffi-2/",
      "html": "<p>Imported from Guinea.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pelvicachromis-roloffi-2/",
      "html": "<p>As usual in Pelvicachromis, the females are the more colourful fish. Males are larger, females stay smaller.</p>"
    }
